node_modules/
# ...and node_modules as a SYMLINK. The trailing slash above matches a directory only, so a
# worktree that borrows the main checkout's install (the documented way to run a commit hook
# where `pnpm install` has not run) leaves a symlink `git add -A` will happily stage. Caught
# 10/09 mid-commit.
node_modules
# Agent worktrees are independent checkouts, never part of this checkout's source.
.claude/worktrees/
# Build jobs, generated copy and seeder receipts in the local workspace.
docs/agents/*
# ...except the three agent-skill config files written by /setup-matt-pocock-skills (13/10/2026).
!docs/agents/issue-tracker.md
!docs/agents/triage-labels.md
!docs/agents/domain.md
data/
# ...except a design export's data/ under vendor/joomla/html: it is contract source, hashed by the
# template's qa.contract.json. The line above kept tracy_base/data/*.json out of git (15/09/2026), and
# with the machine that had them gone, Tracy Base's contracts gate failed everywhere (TCH #1180).
!vendor/joomla/html/*/data/

# Finder junk. One got into the tree on 01/09 (`workers/.DS_Store`, `4004157`) because no line
# blocked it, not through anyone's carelessness. Listed here, it covers every folder.
.DS_Store

# Worker secrets for local dev. These files hold REAL values (`FLEET_ACTOR_SECRET` signs identity
# claims for EVERY person on EVERY site; `SHOPIFY_CLIENT_SECRET` is one secret shared by every
# customer store). They came along with the Worker code from tracy-infra, which ignores them —
# without this line the first commit here would push all of them to GitHub.
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
# ...except the empty template. `.dev.vars.*` above also swallows `.dev.vars.example`, so the
# template must be named again here, or it silently stays out of git and newcomers can't tell what the Worker needs.
!.dev.vars.example
# wrangler run/build output, not definitions.
.wrangler/
# `.env` alone does NOT match `.env.desktop` — each profile has its own env file because
# dsh-passwords pins the gateway port there, and both hold real secrets.
.env
.env.*
# ...except the empty templates for newcomers. Same reason as `.dev.vars.example` above: `.env.*`
# also matches `.env.example`, and a template that can't get into git is a template nobody reads.
!.env*.example
# A second local stand's names and ports (docs/running-locally.md).
deploy/compose.override.yml

# Private keys never go into git. This folder holds things that are NOT environment variables —
# a GitHub App private key, for instance — which `.env.*` above does not cover.
.secrets/
# An operator's local secrets folder at the repo root (SRE, 14/10/2026). Never commit anything in it.
/credentials/
tch/sessions/
tch/storages/
tch/settings.yaml*
tch/.credentials.yaml*
# Images users paste into a chat session, hashed by content. One machine's DATA, possibly
# screenshots with private information — the worst thing to commit by accident. First appeared
# on 31/08 when the `native` profile came into real use.
tch/attachments/
# Model provider's file-list cache; dsh regenerates it when needed.
tch/llm-deepseek/
.teamshare/

tch/.anonymous-user-id

# Electron build output — ~250 MB of binaries, rebuilt with `pnpm --filter @tracy/desktop package`
packages/desktop/tracy-desktop/dist/
# Bundled by build/build-shell.mjs from shell/ and the dsh submodule at start and package time.
packages/desktop/tracy-desktop/src/generated/
# The macOS notification permission addon, built by build/build-native.sh at package time.
packages/desktop/tracy-desktop/src/native/
packages/desktop/tracy-desktop/build/icon.iconset/
packages/desktop/tracy-desktop/build/icon.icns

# Vite build of the design bench (~668 KB), produced by `pnpm build`. UNLIKE a plugin's
# `lib/client.js`, which IS committed because the fleet copies the folder as-is and builds nothing
# there — nobody ships the bench, it only runs on the author's machine. Without this line anyone's
# first `pnpm build` leaves an untracked folder inviting an accidental commit.
packages/dev/tracy-design/dist/
# CMS template zips: built from the committed sources by each package's scripts/build.mjs
packages/cms/tracy-joomla-template/dist/
packages/cms/tracy-wordpress-theme/dist/
packages/cms/tracy-seeder/dist/

# dsh's one-time sign-in token, regenerated on every run — secret, and meaningless on another machine.
tch/profiles/*/.launch-token
# Skill library + design systems built for an agent running LOCALLY (`node scripts/dev-skills.mjs`).
# Generated from `vendor/tracy/od-skill` and `vendor/tracy/od-design-system`, so committing them
# duplicates a library already in the repo. On the fleet, `dsh/Dockerfile` builds the equivalent at
# `/opt/tracy/skills`.
tch/skills/
tch/design-systems
tch/design-catalog.json
tch/craft


# A reference template, NOT a build dependency — which is why it differs from everything else in
# `vendor/`.
#
# `vendor/tracy/dsh-passwords`, `vendor/tracy/dsh-locale-vi`, `vendor/tracy/dsh-better-sidebar`,
# `vendor/tracy/dsh-better-locale`, `vendor/tracy/od-brand-engine`, `vendor/tracy/mattpocock-skills` are TRACKED
# subtrees: since 06/09 they are workspace members or content `dsh/Dockerfile` copies straight into
# the image — no publish step in between — so their code must live in the repo.
# `vendor/tracy/shadcn-admin` is READ-ONLY — look at how it builds layouts, never import a line.
# tracy-infra keeps it out of git for the same reason.
#
# Recreate when needed (the exact commit tracy-infra references):
#   git clone https://github.com/satnaing/shadcn-admin.git vendor/tracy/shadcn-admin
#   git -C vendor/tracy/shadcn-admin checkout e16c87f
vendor/tracy/shadcn-admin/

# `pnpm install` inside the vendor subtree (to run its tests) leaves this lockfile. Upstream uses
# npm with its own `package-lock.json`; committing a second lockfile litters their tree and makes
# the next rebase harder to read.
vendor/tracy/dsh-passwords/pnpm-lock.yaml

# State of the `@tracy/dsh-add-site` host half when run OUTSIDE dsh (tests, manual scripts).
#
# `tokens.ts` and `resume.ts` write to `$DSH_HOME`; without it they fall back to cwd, and the cwd of
# an `npx tsx` run is the repo root. The content is customer-site extension codes and a download
# cursor — none of it belongs in git.
/tracy-add-site/
packages/web/tracy-harness/dist/
# Generated from git by `scripts/gen-ops-cms-snapshot.mjs` right before each tracy-web image build
# (one JSON per environment, with provenance). Not committed: it describes a commit that changes daily.
apps/tracy-web/static/ops-cms/

# Storybook build (`pnpm --filter @tracy/design build-storybook`). It packs every story into one
# minified bundle — committing it recommits all of @tracy/ui in unreadable form, and
# `check-language` trips on Vietnamese text pulled in by the bundle's dependencies.
packages/dev/tracy-design/storybook-static/

# Storybook debug logs left by manual runs.
packages/dev/tracy-design/*.log
__pycache__/

# Local site folders of the one-dsh test bed (packages/tools/tracy-subprocess-docker/dev)
tch/sites/

# The CMS seeder staged for the host-dsh image (scripts/tools/stage-cms-seeder.sh); rebuilt, never committed
packages/fleet/tracy-fleet-operation/dsh/cms/

# The Turnstile SITE key is public by design (it ships in the page HTML); committing it lets
# scripts/deploy.mjs build the page the same from any checkout. The secret lives only in the Worker.
!packages/web/tracy-design-page/.env.production

# wp-tracy-business dossier: two evidence folders live outside the repo and are symlinks on the
# machine; not committed — CI has no target, and oxlint would scan customer JS through the symlink.
tasks/wp-tracy-business/spec/assets
tasks/wp-tracy-business/spec/reference
# `contract.mjs init` moves the old canonical copy here on every run (a local safety net, not code):
# 24 folders after one day of building, and the canonical copy in use is already committed.
tasks/wp-tracy-business/attempts/

# ── Machine-generated, not code (added 15/09/2026 during a tree cleanup) ──────────────
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.dsh-mattskillsdeck-cache/
packages/cms/tracy-emdash-theme-business/server.log
# retired private registry (ADR 0014 §6) — data left on the machine, not for git
infra/registry/
# read-only shadcn-admin clone, same rule as vendor/tracy/shadcn-admin above
vendor/shadcn-admin/
# An unpacked npm package, not a vendor subtree — same rule as the line above. The test is
# IMPORT-NOTE.md: on 23/09, 15 vendors had one, and the only two leaves without one were the line
# above and this one. This tree has `package/` + `package-lock.json` (the `npm pack` layout) and no
# note, so it never came in through the commit-pinned subtree path (ADR 0006). 64 MB, `??` in
# `git status`, so `git add -A` would take all of it — the same trap as `workers/` at the end of this file.
vendor/dsh-mattpocock-skills-deck/
# design-library store generated by the tracy-design plugin at runtime
tch/design-library/

# 🔒 THE WORKER TREE WAS DELETED, AND IT IS STILL ON THE DISK OF ANYONE WHO CHECKED OUT BEFORE THE DELETION.
# `b98f21c8f` (16/09/2026) removed 181 files, −62 924 lines — "nothing in the product runs on them any
# more"; every old door is now answered by `apps/tracy-web` (`src/lanes/route.js` and its sibling routes).
# But `git rm` does not clean an existing checkout's folder: measured on 23/09, one machine still had
# **1471 files / 41 MB**, and with no line blocking it, `git status` lists it as `??` — so **one
# `git add -A` takes the whole tree and revives a buried architecture**, silently, in a commit
# meant to be about something else. Same shape of accident as the submodule pointer in `606c6d82`.
#
# Ignored rather than forcing anyone to delete: the files on disk stay searchable, and `git log -- workers/` keeps the history.
# ⚠ Two files `workers/harness/{src/hosts.js,test/host-agents.test.mjs}` carry timestamps AFTER the
# deletion (20/09), so they look like work in progress — compared byte for byte with the pre-deletion
# copy: **identical**. That was a restore, not anyone's new code.
workers/

# tsc --incremental build-info (CI restores it; see tracy-ci.yml)
.cache/

# Output of `pnpm qa` (manual QA suite runs, stand manifests, fixture secrets).
qa-results/
# dsh-subscriptions runtime state (accounts, quarantine) when a local profile runs the plan card — never commit
tch/subscriptions/

# Turborepo run logs and local cache (turbo.json); never inputs, never committed.
.turbo/

# Pinned gitleaks downloaded by scripts/opensource/install-gitleaks.mjs.
scripts/opensource/.bin/

# Local dev-server logs (one was committed by mistake on 26/10/2026).
.dev-logs/

# A machine's own dsh profile rows (test webroot, local paths); ./run.sh loads it with --patch.
tch/profiles/*/cordis.local.yml
